---
/**
 * Pricing, published.
 *
 * Only 6 of 21 surveyed competitors publish a price at all. That opacity is the
 * biggest opening in this market and it costs us nothing to exploit — so the
 * numbers go on the page, not behind a demo request.
 */
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro'
import { estimatePrice, monthlyPrice, pricingHref, site } from '../lib/site.ts'

const card = 'rounded-xl border border-ink-100 bg-white p-5'
const examples = [2, 5, 10, 20, 40]

/**
 * The estimator's whole state, read out of the URL on the server.
 *
 * No client JavaScript here, which rules out a live slider — and that turns out
 * to be the better answer anyway. `/pricing?trucks=12` renders the same thing
 * for whoever opens it, so the number survives being texted to the partner who
 * signs the checks; the back button walks the sizes he tried; and it works on
 * one bar at a truck stop. Same doctrine as `?show=` on the dashboard and
 * `?kind=` on the fleet list.
 */
const estimate = estimatePrice(Astro.url.searchParams.get('trucks'))
const maxQuoted = site.pricing.maxQuotedTrucks

// What goes back into the number box. A clamped or refused value must NOT come
// back as the thing we would not price: the box is the receipt for what the
// page actually did with the URL, so `?trucks=0` has to show the 1 we used.
const typed =
  estimate.state === 'priced' || estimate.state === 'oversize' ? String(estimate.trucks) : ''

// The stepper, with no JavaScript to step with: one truck up and one truck down
// are just two more URLs. Only the bottom end is dead — a link to `?trucks=0`
// would bounce off the clamp and look broken. The top end deliberately is NOT
// capped: stepping up from the last quoted size lands on the "talk to us"
// panel, which is the answer to "what happens above this", and a greyed-out +
// would leave that question hanging with nowhere to tap.
const fewer = estimate.state === 'priced' && estimate.trucks > 1 ? estimate.trucks - 1 : null

const stepOn =
  'flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-ink-100 bg-white text-xl font-medium transition hover:bg-ink-50'
const stepOff =
  'flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-ink-100 text-xl text-ink-300'
const pill = 'rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium transition'

const included = [
  'Every federal and California deadline we track',
  'Unlimited drivers, trucks and trailers',
  'Unlimited users, so the whole office can log in at no extra cost',
  'Email alerts, on your schedule. Text messages are coming later',
  'Loads, trips and dispatch',
  'The printable proof packet',
  'Your carrier record from FMCSA, checked again every week',
]

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Why per truck and not per user?',
    a: 'Two people need to be in this system: the owner and the person who runs the office. Charging per user would punish you for that. Every plan has unlimited users. If you hire a second dispatcher, your bill stays the same.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when I add or sell a truck?',
    // Said out loud because the estimator now shows it: a three-truck fleet
    // adding a fourth sees no change at all, and copy promising "six dollars"
    // would read as the page contradicting its own calculator.
    a: `Your bill goes up or down by $${site.pricing.perTruck}. If you are on the $${site.pricing.floor} minimum, it does not change at all until your fifth truck. There are no tiers and no jump at any size. We did that on purpose. A price jump would give you a reason to hide a truck from your compliance software, and neither of us wants that.`,
  },
  {
    q: `What if I run more than ${maxQuoted} trucks?`,
    a: `The price is the same: $${site.pricing.perTruck} a truck, and there is no higher tier. The calculator stops at ${maxQuoted} because that is the biggest fleet we have built and tested for. We do not want to give you a number we have never sold at. Start the trial and talk to us. Either way, nothing is billed for ${site.pricing.trialDays} days.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What counts as a truck?',
    a: 'A power unit: a tractor or a straight truck. Trailers are free and drivers are free. Count the ones with an engine.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a contract?',
    a: 'No. You pay monthly and you can cancel any month. If you leave, you can export your records first. They are yours.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is not included?',
    a: 'We do not file anything for you. We cannot run your Drug and Alcohol Clearinghouse queries, because the rules do not allow us to use your login. Be careful with anyone who offers. And we are not an ELD. We track your dates, remind you, and keep your proof.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you charge to get set up?',
    a: 'There is no setup fee. We read what the federal record already knows from your DOT number. You add the dates that are only in your office. That is about one evening of work, one time.',
  },
]
---

<Public
  title="Pricing"
  description={`$${site.pricing.perTruck} per truck per month, $${site.pricing.floor} minimum, unlimited users. No contract, ${site.pricing.trialDays} days free, no card needed.`}
>
  <section class="border-b border-ink-100 bg-ink-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
        ${site.pricing.perTruck} a truck, a month. That is the whole price.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-500">
        The minimum is ${site.pricing.floor} a month, so small fleets can afford it. Unlimited
        users. No contract. {site.pricing.trialDays} days free, and you do not need a card to
        start.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    {/* clears the sticky header, which otherwise sits on top of the
    answer every link in this card jumps to. */}
    <div id="estimate" class="rounded-2xl border border-ink-100 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-5">
        <div class="max-w-md">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What would it cost you?</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
            Count power units: tractors and straight trucks. Trailers, drivers and office staff
            are free, so do not count them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <form method="GET" action="/pricing" class="flex items-end gap-2">
          <label class="block w-32 text-sm font-medium">
            How many trucks?
            {/* No max= on purpose. The browser would silently refuse to submit a
            bigger fleet, and a 60-truck carrier deserves the honest "talk to
            us" answer rather than a form that appears broken. */}
            <input
              type="number"
              name="trucks"
              value={typed}
              min="1"
              step="1"
              required
              inputmode="numeric"
              placeholder="10"
              class="mt-1 block w-full rounded-lg border border-ink-100 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-base tabular-nums outline-none focus:border-brand-500 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-brand-500/20"
            />
          </label>
          <button
            type="submit"
            class="rounded-lg bg-brand-600 px-5 py-2.5 font-medium text-white transition hover:bg-brand-700"
          >
            Show me
          </button>
        </form>
      </div>

      {/* One tap answers it for most visitors, so the common sizes are links and
      nobody has to type anything at all. */}
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="mr-1 text-sm text-ink-500">Common fleets</span>
        {
          examples.map((n) => (
            <a
              href={pricingHref(n)}
              class:list={[
                pill,
                estimate.state === 'priced' && estimate.trucks === n
                  ? 'bg-brand-500/10 text-brand-700'
                  : 'text-ink-500 hover:bg-ink-50 hover:text-ink-900',
              ]}
            >
              {n} trucks
            </a>
          ))
        }
        {
          estimate.state !== 'none' && (
            <a href="/pricing" class:list={[pill, 'text-ink-500 hover:bg-ink-50']}>
              Clear
            </a>
          )
        }
      </div>

      {
        estimate.state === 'priced' && (
          <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/30 bg-brand-500/[0.04] p-5 sm:p-6">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                {fewer ? (
                  <a href={pricingHref(fewer)} aria-label={`Price ${fewer} trucks`} class={stepOn}>
                    −
                  </a>
                ) : (
                  <span aria-hidden="true" class={stepOff}>
                    −
                  </span>
                )}
                <span class="w-24 text-center text-lg font-medium tabular-nums">
                  {estimate.trucks} {estimate.trucks === 1 ? 'truck' : 'trucks'}
                </span>
                <a
                  href={pricingHref(estimate.trucks + 1)}
                  aria-label={`Price ${estimate.trucks + 1} trucks`}
                  class={stepOn}
                >
                  +
                </a>
              </div>
              <p>
                <span class="text-5xl font-semibold tabular-nums">${estimate.monthly}</span>
                <span class="text-ink-500"> a month</span>
              </p>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500">
              <span class="tabular-nums">${estimate.effectivePerTruck.toFixed(2)}</span> per truck.
              {estimate.onFloor
                ? ` You pay the $${site.pricing.floor} minimum until your fifth truck. The fifth
                  truck is the first one that adds a dollar.`
                : ` Each truck after this adds $${site.pricing.perTruck}. There are no tiers on the
                  way up.`}
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-500">
              That is the whole bill at that size. Unlimited users, unlimited drivers and trailers,
              no setup fee, no contract.
            </p>
            {/* The one thing this page does NOT know, said next to the number
            rather than under the fold: we priced a number he typed, and the
            bill follows the units actually on the account. */}
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink-500">
              This price is for the number you typed. Your real bill counts the power units on your
              account. Add or remove one and the bill changes by ${site.pricing.perTruck} that
              month. Nothing is charged for the first {site.pricing.trialDays} days.
            </p>
            <a
              href="/check"
              class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-medium text-brand-600 hover:underline"
            >
              Start your {site.pricing.trialDays} free days →
            </a>
          </div>
        )
      }

      {
        estimate.state === 'oversize' && (
          <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-blue-100 bg-blue-50 p-5 sm:p-6">
            {/* Blue, not amber: this is a standing fact about us, not a clock. */}
            <p class="font-medium text-blue-900">
              We do not quote <span class="tabular-nums">{estimate.trucks}</span> trucks on this
              page.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-blue-900/80">
              The price does not change and there is no tier above you. It is still $
              {site.pricing.perTruck} a truck. But {maxQuoted} trucks is the biggest fleet we have
              built and tested for. If we multiplied past that, we would be giving you a number we
              have never sold at. We would rather tell you now than take back a quote on the first
              call.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-blue-900/80">
              Start with your DOT number and we will talk before anything is billed, or{' '}
              <a href={pricingHref(maxQuoted)} class="font-medium text-blue-900 underline">
                see the price at {maxQuoted} trucks
              </a>
              .
            </p>
          </div>
        )
      }

      {/* Same treatment /check gives a bad USDOT number: say we could not read
      it, keep the rest of the page standing. An unreadable size must never
      render a price — a made-up number here is worse than no number. */}
      {
        estimate.state === 'unreadable' && (
          <p class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">
            We could not read that as a number of trucks. Type a whole number, like 12, and we
            will show you the price.
          </p>
        )
      }

      {
        estimate.state === 'none' && (
          <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-ink-100 p-8 text-center">
            <p class="mx-auto max-w-md text-sm text-ink-500">
              Pick a size, or type your own. The price you land on stays in the web address, so
              you can send the link to whoever signs the checks.
            </p>
          </div>
        )
      }
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr]">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-brand-500/30 bg-brand-500/[0.04] p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-widest text-brand-600 uppercase">One plan</p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <span class="text-5xl font-semibold tabular-nums">${site.pricing.perTruck}</span>
          <span class="text-ink-500"> per truck, per month</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          Billed monthly. Minimum ${site.pricing.floor}/month.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/check"
          class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-xl bg-brand-600 px-7 py-3.5 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-brand-700"
        >
          Start with your DOT number →
        </a>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-ink-500">No card needed. Nothing to cancel if you walk away.</p>
      </div>

      <div class={card}>
        <p class="font-medium">What that works out to</p>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="border-b border-ink-100 text-left text-xs tracking-wide text-ink-500 uppercase">
              <tr>
                <th class="py-2 font-medium">Trucks</th>
                <th class="py-2 text-right font-medium">Per month</th>
                <th class="py-2 text-right font-medium">Per truck</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-ink-100">
              {
                examples.map((n) => {
                  const m = monthlyPrice(n)
                  // Each row is also a way into the estimator, so the ladder and
                  // the calculator can never drift apart — same numbers, one
                  // function, and clicking a row just asks it the question.
                  const here = estimate.state === 'priced' && estimate.trucks === n
                  return (
                    <tr class:list={[here && 'bg-brand-500/[0.06]']}>
                      <td class="py-2.5 tabular-nums">
                        <a href={pricingHref(n, { fromBelow: true })} class="font-medium text-brand-600 hover:underline">
                          {n}
                        </a>
                      </td>
                      <td class="py-2.5 text-right font-medium tabular-nums">${m}</td>
                      <td class="py-2.5 text-right tabular-nums text-ink-500">
                        ${(m / n).toFixed(2)}
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  )
                })
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-500">
          Small fleets pay the ${site.pricing.floor} minimum, so the price per truck starts higher
          and comes down to ${site.pricing.perTruck}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class={card}>
        <p class="font-medium">Everything is included</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          {
            included.map((i) => (
              <li class="flex gap-2">
                <svg
                  class="mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-emerald-600"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="2.5"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="m5 13 4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <span>{i}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-500">
          Every size gets the same product. Nothing is locked behind a bigger plan.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class={card}>
        <p class="font-medium">How that compares</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-500">
          A fleet with 10 trucks pays{' '}
          <strong class="tabular-nums text-ink-900">${monthlyPrice(10)}</strong> a month here.
          Dispatch software built for fleets your size usually starts around{' '}
          <strong>$290 a month, charged per user</strong>, on a one-year contract. Most of them
          will not tell you the price without a sales call.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-500">
          You probably already pay $25 to $40 per truck each month for ELDs. This costs less than
          a quarter of that.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-300">
          Competitor prices come from published rate cards and public reviews, as of September
          2026. If a vendor shows us a price is out of date, we will fix it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-ink-100 bg-ink-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Questions about the price</h2>
      <dl class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        {
          faqs.map((f) => (
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink-100 bg-white p-5">
              <dt class="font-medium">{f.q}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">{f.a}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
</Public>
